ct such that <MATH_0004>\nis a neighbourhood of <MATH_0005>. For every <MATH_0006> we can find\na finite subset <MATH_0007> and quasi-compact\n<MATH_0008>, <MATH_0009> such that <MATH_0010>\nis a neighbourhood of <MATH_0011>. Since <MATH_0012> is quasi-compact we find\na finite collection <MATH_0013> such that\n<MATH_0014>\nThen we find that\n<MATH_0015>\nis a neighbourhood of <MATH_0016>.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nProof of (3). Let <MATH_0017> be a point. Let <MATH_0018> be its image.\nChoose <MATH_0019> and quasi-compact subsets\n<MATH_0020> such that <MATH_0021> is a\nneighbourhood of <MATH_0022>. Choose a quasi-compact neighbourhood <MATH_0023>\nof <MATH_0024> which maps into the quasi-compact neighbourhood\n<MATH_0025> of <MATH_0026>. Then\n<MATH_0027> is a\nquasi-compact subset and <MATH_0028> is the image of the map\n<MATH_0029>. Hence the base change is a\nqc covering and the proof is finished.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5f777cf073eeeb2d8f00f31418b051df8efe42c54592f0fa51e9f0c926af5540", "unit_id": "tag:09X1:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "09WY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\textit{LC}$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$\\textit{LC}$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-section-proper}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fbf612caac7491e67c8a23a4492de7c8496d34e84102289385c6a4433ad93380", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ddb27c6b4bf843759b7b3bcedcb367a595bfa136ae33155a50a8ba613b295cbf", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSince all objects of <MATH_0001> are Hausdorff any morphism\n<MATH_0002> of <MATH_0003> is a separated continuous map\nof topological spaces. Hence <MATH_0004> is a proper map of topological spaces\nif and only if <MATH_0005> is universally closed. See discussion in\nTopology, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3ba948a8f6742292a99f8c43b1fad3f1d34f32de239abd000cb4eac6a46623ca", "unit_id": "tag:09WY:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "09WY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{LC}$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{f : X \\to Y\\}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-proper-surjective-is-qc-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:97489345e834be98d8ea41efe02c23466ea97f96f119ab855bcb7271c1a33dd8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d0a1a1ad49fb04ae6fa6e58acfaa217309ce4c737681bd834f9beaa9cc5e86cb", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of <MATH_0002>.\nIf <MATH_0003> is proper and surjective, then <MATH_0004>\nis a qc covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:91278237cc8f64acaefd85e906da13b2383aba4199f602dcfc0a119987576ca9", "unit_id": "tag:09X5:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "09WY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$y \\in Y$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in X_y$", "MATH_0003": "$E_x \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$x \\in U_x \\subset E_x$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$X_y$", "MATH_0007": "$x_1, \\ldots, x_n \\in X_y$", "MATH_0008": "$X_y \\subset U_{x_1} \\cup \\ldots \\cup U_{x_n}$", "MATH_0009": "$f(E_{x_1}) \\cup \\ldots \\cup f(E_{x_n})$", "MATH_0010": "$y$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "MATH_0012": "$Z = f(X \\setminus U_{x_1} \\cup \\ldots \\cup U_{x_n})$", "MATH_0013": "$Y$", "MATH_0014": "$y$", "MATH_0015": "$f$", "MATH_0016": "$Y \\setminus Z$", "MATH_0017": "$f(E_{x_1}) \\cup \\ldots \\cup f(E_{x_n})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-theorem-characterize-proper}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6615a1e4e60307883abfb90a746b43fb1853a370502e130665b0513cc84005d9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:418ead35030ce59c11d5bc2a91f51d7709acc06eedf3f5ae2977782b9ce57747", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a point. For each <MATH_0002> choose a quasi-compact\nneighbourhood <MATH_0003>. Choose <MATH_0004> open.\nSince <MATH_0005> is proper the fibre <MATH_0006> is quasi-compact and we find\n<MATH_0007> such that\n<MATH_0008>.\nWe claim that <MATH_0009> is a neighbourhood of\n<MATH_0010>. Namely, as <MATH_0011> is closed\n(Topology, Theorem <REF_0001>)\nwe see that <MATH_0012>\nis a closed subset of <MATH_0013> not containing <MATH_0014>. As <MATH_0015> is surjective\nwe see that <MATH_0016> is contained in\n<MATH_0017> as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:84ed5f761cbe90bf74627d46a0d5ac7e0442f406e604d22811e6caf7d22be06f", "unit_id": "tag:09X5:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "09WY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\textit{LC}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{LC}_{qc}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-qc}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2ab5e3c46753b991b5e77115bb264e783172b710340b8646922507af23a1f1c5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:79731868be0464327b7e948d94d0e1ae73d48bf4801ff092cce708acbfe74944", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nBesides some set theoretic issues Lemma <REF_0001> shows that\n<MATH_0001> with the collection of qc coverings forms a site.\nWe will denote this site (suitably modified to overcome the\nset theoretical issues)\n<MATH_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5c7f2620623c9513f09fa18464ef23366c720c8e624b0455ebc84682c15a23da", "unit_id": "tag:09WY:prose-0005"}
